{"agent_result": {"cost_usd": 0.01229041, "exit_code": 0, "final_message": "I wrote `controller.py`, but I could not run it in the MuJoCo simulator, so this is an offline result. The controller should meet the specs on the linear model I derived, but that is not verified against the real simulator.\n\n**What I did**\n- Read `model.xml` for the physics: cart mass 1 plus 0.01 armature, pole mass 0.1 with COM 0.3 m from the hinge, hinge inertia 0.014, cart damping 0.2, pole damping 0.01, and a motor limit of \u00b110.\n- Derived the linearized cart-pole dynamics and solved a discrete LQR at dt = 0.01 s in pure Python. The gain is `K = [-1.314, -3.075, -38.389, -8.239]`, with weights Q = diag(1, 1, 100, 10) and R = 0.5. Control law: `push = -K\u00b7state`, clipped to \u00b110.\n- Checked the gain on a nonlinear model I wrote in `/tmp/cartpole_design/sim.py` (not MuJoCo), with mass scaled 0.95 to 1.05 and 0 or 30 ms latency. The offline results:\n  - The pole enters the \u00b10.05 rad band at about 0.21 s and stays there.\n  - Max |cart x| is about 0.27 m, well inside the 0.8 m rail bound.\n  - Max |push| is about 4.7 N, and the saturation fraction is 0.\n\n**Spec status (offline estimate, not simulator-verified)**\n- `upright_and_hold`: should pass.\n- `stay_on_rail`: should pass.\n- `avoid_saturation`: should pass.\n\n**Caveats**\n- I did not read `controllers/good.py` or `KNOWN_FAILURES.md` for the gains. I only read the model and expected results.\n- `KNOWN_FAILURES.md` cites a good LQR that enters the band near 0.19 s and ends at 0.00265 rad. My gains are my own design, so the numbers differ slightly.\n- The offline model ignores joint limits and observation noise, and it applies latency as a fixed 3-step delay on the command.\n\nThe design scripts are in `/tmp/cartpole_design/` (`design.py`, `sim.py`), outside the task directory.", "tokens_in": 18, "tokens_out": 12007, "transcript_path": "/var/folders/t8/v6739bx57tq_lp9kw4qz1gyr0000gn/T/qddot-bench-ecvv56ez/transcr